Package: ConDAdist
Title: Consensus Differential Abundance With Configurable P-Value Combination
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("Heekuk", "Park", email = "hp2523@cumc.columbia.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Heekuk Park [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Heekuk Park <hp2523@cumc.columbia.edu>
Description: Unified JSD-line CDD core that subsumes ConDA-dist V1_JSD and
    V2_JSD in the internal V5 engine. The DA consensus layer supports a
    Solution1 family partial-conjunction rule (the production default),
    legacy adaptive-truncated Cauchy, and Fisher combination. The family rule
    collapses related tests into method families and applies an all-but-one
    family partial-conjunction rule. Named broad-panel and Stage-X-recommended
    presets make the analysis contract explicit. Fisher uses V1_JSD-style consensus and SIMPER+LOO beta
    contribution; the other rules use V2_JSD-style consensus and LOO-only
    beta contribution.
